le": "HPI m/m", "impact": "Low"}, {"time_utc": "09:00", "currency": "USD", "title": "S&P/CS Composite-20 HPI y/y", "impact": "Low"}], "editorial": "Cable sits at 1.3301 as Tuesday's session gets underway, trading just beneath what the structure map identifies as a prior reaction zone clustered around 1.3303. The daily chart tells a story of a pair that ran hard into mid-July and has since spent the better part of two weeks unwinding that move in a measured, if persistent, fashion.\n\nThe structure story begins with that July 15th surge \u2014 a daily candle that stretched from the 1.3378 area all the way to a high of 1.3558, the strongest single-session move in the dataset. What followed was a textbook drift lower: a sequence of lower closes that has now retraced roughly two-thirds of that impulsive leg. The pair has pulled back through the 1.3482 prior reaction zone without meaningful defence, and price is now compressing just above the 1.3303 zone \u2014 a level that has registered three prior touches and now sits directly overhead on the H1 picture. The broader trend from late June remains constructive on the daily timeframe, but the recent sequence of lower highs and lower closes since the 15th introduces genuine ambiguity, which is reflected in the desk's neutral bias.\n\nOn the hourly chart, the picture is one of gradual stabilisation after a sharp sell-off through the early hours of Monday's Asian session, which drove price down to a low of 1.3284. Since the European open this morning, H1 candles have been grinding higher in a tight range, with each successive hour posting a marginally higher low. The 1.3303 zone is acting as a ceiling on an intraday basis \u2014 price has tested it from below twice in the last two hours without conviction. The H1 structure suggests the pair is in a coiling phase, with neither side yet willing to commit.\n\nToday's calendar is USD-centric and weighted towards the afternoon. CB Consumer Confidence at 10:00 UTC is the most consequential release, carrying medium-impact status. A materially stronger-than-expected reading could reinforce dollar demand and apply renewed downward pressure on Cable, potentially dragging price back towards the 1.3284\u20131.3290 area tested overnight. A softer print could provide the catalyst for a more sustained push back through the 1.3303 zone. The morning cluster of lower-tier USD data \u2014 ADP weekly employment, goods trade balance, and housing metrics \u2014 is unlikely to move the needle significantly in isolation, though a consistent directional skew across the batch could set a tone ahead of the confidence number.\n\nThe read shifts materially on a clean daily close above 1.3303, which would suggest the prior reaction zone has flipped from resistance to support and opens the path back towards 1.3452. Conversely, a sustained break and hold beneath 1.3284 \u2014 the overnight low \u2014 would represent the level that invalidates any near-term recovery scenario and brings the 1.3141 support zone back into the structural conversation.\n\nThis is editorial analysis, not financial advice. Trading involves substantial risk of loss.", "sample": false}